WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.317 --> 00:00:17.863
Ben got out of his sleeping bag and floated through the classroom door.

2
00:00:19.523 --> 00:00:22.865
Ahead of him the shadowy figure was creeping down the corridor.

3
00:00:24.265 --> 00:00:25.486
Ben floated after him.

4
00:00:25.506 --> 00:00:29.348
"Who is that?"

5
00:00:29.708 --> 00:00:30.188
he thought.

6
00:00:31.356 --> 00:00:33.438
The figure was holding some sort of book.

7
00:00:33.458 --> 00:00:38.923
"Hey!" Ben called out, and the figure whirled around in surprise.

8
00:00:38.943 --> 00:00:41.945
"Waldo!" Ben exclaimed.

9
00:00:41.965 --> 00:00:45.568
"What are you doing?"

10
00:00:45.588 --> 00:00:48.571
"Phew! Thank goodness it's you!"

11
00:00:49.131 --> 00:00:50.973
Waldo looked relieved to see Ben.

12
00:00:50.993 --> 00:00:54.136
"I couldn't sleep," the wizard explained.

13
00:00:54.156 --> 00:00:56.197
"I kept thinking about Uncle Tut.

14
00:00:56.718 --> 00:00:58.900
I promised Cleo that I'd help her wake him up.

15
00:01:00.168 --> 00:01:01.609
I've brought my spell book this time.

16
00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:03.070
I'm sure I can wake him up."

17
00:01:04.231 --> 00:01:06.232
Ben didn't want to hurt Waldo's feelings.

18
00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:13.598
But the wizard's spells rarely worked, and so many things had already gone wrong on this field trip.

19
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.002
Waldo, do you think a spell is safe?"

20
00:01:20.462 --> 00:01:21.603
Ben asked carefully.

21
00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:24.525
"I mean, what if you make a mistake?

22
00:01:24.946 --> 00:01:31.082
Dr. Bones is already furious at us, and Miss Bungle said—" "It'll be fine," Waldo said.

23
00:01:31.102 --> 00:01:33.543
"It can't hurt to try, right?"

24
00:01:33.563 --> 00:01:40.528
"Um Ben didn't know what to say, so he just nodded slowly.

25
00:01:40.548 --> 00:01:45.912
"Okay, well, I'll come with you, just in case something happens.

26
00:01:46.513 --> 00:01:48.574
How are we going to get to Uncle Tut?

27
00:01:49.134 --> 00:01:52.197
Al Normal said he locked the main entrance at eight o'clock."

28
00:01:53.277 --> 00:01:57.700
"I bet we can go through the construction site, if we're careful," Waldo said.

29
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:02.022
"I saw some construction workers entering the museum from the education wing."

30
00:02:04.383 --> 00:02:06.264
"Okay," Ben said with a shrug.

31
00:02:06.284 --> 00:02:07.724
"I guess we can try."

32
00:02:07.745 --> 00:02:14.367
He and Waldo slipped downstairs to the first-floor construction area.

33
00:02:18.429 --> 00:02:22.170
As they got closer, they noticed someone else had gotten there first.

34
00:02:26.028 --> 00:02:26.788
Ben whispered.

35
00:02:26.808 --> 00:02:30.570
"What are you doing here?"

36
00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:34.712
"I can't wait until morning," Cleo whispered back.

37
00:02:34.732 --> 00:02:37.233
"I need to rescue my uncle now!"

38
00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:39.814
Waldo held up his spell book.

39
00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.334
"Don't worry.

40
00:02:41.554 --> 00:02:42.615
We'll figure this out."

41
00:02:44.556 --> 00:02:46.036
Ben looked around uneasily.

42
00:02:46.056 --> 00:02:49.698
"Let's go," he whispered.

43
00:02:49.718 --> 00:02:51.298
"Before we get caught."

44
00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:54.800
The three monsters examined the construction area.

45
00:02:55.932 --> 00:03:02.278
It was still filled with scaffolding, tools, buckets, partially finished walls, and other obstacles.

46
00:03:03.059 --> 00:03:06.622
Ben knew he'd have no trouble getting through, but his friends might.

47
00:03:08.323 --> 00:03:10.065
"I'll go first," Ben said.

48
00:03:10.085 --> 00:03:13.367
"I'll try to warn you guys about obstacles in our way."

49
00:03:14.108 --> 00:03:18.352
Cleo and Waldo nodded, and Ben floated into the construction area.

50
00:03:24.616 --> 00:03:30.219
"These workers are really sloppy," he whispered to Waldo and Cleo, who were following close behind.

51
00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:33.881
"They've left buckets and tools everywhere.

52
00:03:34.141 --> 00:03:34.842
Watch your step."

53
00:03:36.263 --> 00:03:38.144
"We will," Waldo replied.

54
00:03:38.164 --> 00:03:41.966
"Ouch!" said Cleo.

55
00:03:42.366 --> 00:03:43.347
Ben whirled around.

56
00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:44.227
"What's wrong?"

57
00:03:45.248 --> 00:03:47.049
"My wrapping got caught on that nail."

58
00:03:47.549 --> 00:03:48.670
She laughed nervously.

59
00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:52.412
"It would be really embarrassing if I unraveled."

60
00:03:55.756 --> 00:03:57.097
They started forward again.

61
00:03:57.117 --> 00:04:03.700
"Whoops!" said Waldo as something crashed loudly to the floor.

62
00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.041
"What's wrong now?"

63
00:04:05.441 --> 00:04:09.323
Ben turned and saw Waldo lying on the ground, holding his ankle.

64
00:04:09.343 --> 00:04:14.006
"I tripped on something," Waldo said.

65
00:04:14.026 --> 00:04:16.327
"I twisted my ankle."

66
00:04:16.828 --> 00:04:17.448
He rubbed it.

67
00:04:17.468 --> 00:04:22.291
"Ouch." "Can you stand?"

68
00:04:22.711 --> 00:04:23.471
Ben asked.

69
00:04:23.491 --> 00:04:27.017
"Sure. I—Yow!"

70
00:04:27.597 --> 00:04:31.199
Waldo yelped as he stood, and his leg buckled under him.

71
00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:33.560
Cleo looked worried.

72
00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.822
"I think you sprained your ankle, Waldo," she said.

73
00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:37.842
"Or worse.

74
00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:39.403
We'll have to go back."

75
00:04:39.423 --> 00:04:42.205
"No!" Waldo protested.

76
00:04:42.225 --> 00:04:44.406
"We can't give up on Uncle Tut."

77
00:04:47.348 --> 00:04:49.709
"Look at you, Waldo," Cleo whispered.

78
00:04:49.729 --> 00:04:51.009
"You can't walk.

79
00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:55.412
And if we get caught "I can keep going," Ben said.

80
00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.241
"I can move much more quickly than you guys.

81
00:04:58.741 --> 00:05:00.221
I can wake Uncle Tut on my own."

82
00:05:01.161 --> 00:05:02.182
Cleo looked torn.

83
00:05:02.202 --> 00:05:03.542
"Are you sure, Ben?"

84
00:05:04.042 --> 00:05:04.642
she asked.

85
00:05:05.363 --> 00:05:06.183
Ben shrugged.

86
00:05:06.203 --> 00:05:07.583
"I'll try my best."

87
00:05:07.603 --> 00:05:10.804
"Thanks," Cleo said.

88
00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.105
She flashed him a grateful smile.

89
00:05:13.125 --> 00:05:15.605
"I'll take Waldo back upstairs.

90
00:05:15.985 --> 00:05:17.266
I have some extra wrapping.

91
00:05:17.746 --> 00:05:20.407
I bet I can wrap his ankle without Miss Bungle or Mr.

92
00:05:20.447 --> 00:05:21.507
Freaky finding out."

93
00:05:25.632 --> 00:05:26.252
"Good luck!"

94
00:05:26.672 --> 00:05:30.393
Waldo whispered as Ben continued floating through the construction site.

95
00:05:31.454 --> 00:05:36.395
Without the other two monsters slowing him down, Ben quickly made his way into the main part of

96
00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:37.075
the museum.

97
00:05:39.176 --> 00:05:41.116
He floated toward the Egyptian display.

98
00:05:41.997 --> 00:05:46.378
But before he could enter, he saw two figures sneaking into the exhibit.

99
00:05:46.398 --> 00:05:50.439
"That's interesting," Ben thought.

100
00:05:50.459 --> 00:05:53.880
"Some other students are sneaking around the museum."

101
00:05:57.344 --> 00:05:59.545
Ben floated toward a papyrus display.

102
00:06:00.665 --> 00:06:05.606
Now he could see two zombies prowling around, whispering furiously to each other.

103
00:06:09.327 --> 00:06:13.708
As Ben drew closer, he spotted something glinting in their pale hands.

104
00:06:13.728 --> 00:06:16.149
"Huh," Ben thought.

105
00:06:16.169 --> 00:06:17.850
"What is that?

106
00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:22.031
It looks like gold—" He gasped out loud.

107
00:06:22.611 --> 00:06:23.571
It was jewelry.

108
00:06:23.591 --> 00:06:26.552
"Yikes!" he thought.

109
00:06:27.117 --> 00:06:29.685
"Those zombies haven't come to help Uncle Tut.

110
00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:32.896
They're stealing the jewels from the Egyptian exhibit!"
